<section class="section wrap" id="experience"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">03 / PROFESSIONAL PERSPECTIVE</span><span class="mini">RESEARCH RIGOUR. OPERATIONAL AWARENESS.</span></div><div class="experience-grid"><div><h2>Engineering mindset.<br><em>Practical experience.</em></h2><p class="muted">My background spans civil engineering, transport modelling, university teaching and finance operations. Across these settings, the common thread is structured analysis and clear communication.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/ahmed-madhoun/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Explore my professional profile ↗</a></div><div class="experience-list"><article><span class="mini">RESEARCH & TEACHING / WUT</span><h3>Making complex systems understandable.</h3><p>Doctoral research in freight transport, alongside teaching experience in engineering graphics and descriptive geometry.</p></article><article><span class="mini">FINANCE OPERATIONS / ACCENTURE</span><h3>Precision in day-to-day delivery.</h3><p>Experience in accounts receivable and cash collections, operational reporting, escalations, month-end support and training colleagues.</p></article><article><span class="mini">TRANSPORT ENGINEERING / ACADEMIC FOUNDATION</span><h3>From infrastructure to network performance.</h3><p>A civil engineering foundation and master’s work modelling Wrocław’s transport system with PTV Visum, followed by microscopic corridor simulation with PTV Vissim.</p></article></div></div><div class="capabilities"><span>PTV Vissim</span><span>PTV Visum</span><span>Transport modelling</span><span>Data analysis</span><span>Excel & reporting</span><span>Technical communication</span></div></section>
<section class="agenda" id="agenda"><div class="wrap section"><div class="section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">04 / THE NEXT CHAPTER</span><span class="mini">RESEARCH AGENDA · 2026–2028</span></div><div class="agenda-intro"><h2>From promising questions<br>to <em>defensible evidence.</em></h2><p>The next phase focuses on larger datasets, calibrated models and careful validation. These are research objectives, not completed results.</p></div><div class="agenda-items"><article><span>01 / 2026–2027</span><h3>Build the evidence.</h3><p>Develop selected Warsaw corridor models and examine passenger-induced freight penalties under mixed-traffic conditions, supported by an awarded research grant.</p></article><article><span>02 / 2027</span><h3>Test what holds.</h3><p>Validate models, compare candidate indicators against simpler baselines and investigate delay, reliability and relevant emissions outcomes.</p></article><article><span>03 / 2027–2028</span><h3>Connect the findings.</h3><p>Assess sensitivity and uncertainty, bring results together and develop a coherent doctoral contribution. Dissertation submission is targeted for September 2028.</p></article></div><div class="recognition"><span class="mini">RECOGNITION</span><p>2026 WUT scientific competition recognition <span>↗</span> Awarded 2026–2027 mixed-traffic freight research grant</p></div></div></section>
